+# Unverified working checkpoint
+
+Base: `e54523517d0f03e58352e647c403a5af3e525a57`.
+Branch: `research/continuous-20261110-crt-control`.
+Package: `research/encoded-balanced-crt-entry/`.
+Recorded 2026-11-10 16:26 UTC. This is a recovery checkpoint, not a reviewed
+contribution or publication approval.
+
+## Executed
+
+`python -I -B research/encoded-balanced-crt-entry/verify.py --write-result`
+completed with `PASS_ENCODED_BALANCED_CRT_ENTRY nodes=14 owned_roles=78`.
+Four actual-source fixtures cover d=2,4,8; nonzero node starts; changing
+half-size; changing numerical precision; invalid left coordinates and
+padded right coordinates. Runtime geometry/decode functions in the new
+frontend are poisoned, and Port/Word/Arena constructors and Word.inspect
+are sealed after the fixed initial inventory is acquired. The unchanged
+Entry and numeric producer actually run. All source bytes/head restore,
+and all78 owned histories retire blank after complete traversal.
+
+The oracle independently solves the small CRT congruences by enumeration.
+Its decoded values are observer-only and never enter runtime control.
+The current receipt is preliminary and may change when controls are added.
+
+## Not yet verified
+
+The universal invariant and full source-operation bounds are not written
+or independently reviewed. The proposed C M² frontend bound, complete
+retained envelope, shape-rejection cleanup, early close, fault detection,
+source pins, package metadata and optimized replay remain outstanding.
+No complete CRT row/ROM/payload permutation, binary admission, complete
+assumption discharge or kappa improvement is claimed.
+
+## Next
+
+Add source pins and negative controls; prove the encoded cursor/half-size
+invariant and all lifecycle costs; run read-only normal/optimized replays;
+obtain a separate source/mathematical review. The immediate existing replay:
+
+```sh
+python -I -B research/encoded-balanced-crt-entry/verify.py
+```
